      en: `<p>Registers are small, directly accessible storage locations inside the CPU. Memory is a larger addressable storage area. LOAD moves data from memory into a register; STORE writes it back.</p>`,
      fr: `<p>Les registres sont de petits emplacements de stockage directement accessibles à l'intérieur du CPU. La mémoire est une zone de stockage adressable plus grande. LOAD déplace les données de la mémoire vers un registre ; STORE les réécrit.</p>`,
      es: `<p>Los registros son pequeñas ubicaciones de almacenamiento directamente accesibles dentro de la CPU. La memoria es un área de almacenamiento direccionable más grande. LOAD mueve datos de la memoria a un registro; STORE los vuelve a escribir.</p>`,
    },
    docCmpBody: {
      en: `<p>CMP does not need to store a result in a general-purpose register. Instead, it records whether the two operands are equal in the zero flag. JZ can then use that condition to choose between continuing sequentially and jumping to a label.</p>
        <div class="formula-box">CMP A, B → ZF = (A === B) → JZ LABEL</div>`,
      fr: `<p>CMP n'a pas besoin de stocker un résultat dans un registre à usage général. Il enregistre plutôt si les deux opérandes sont égaux dans le drapeau zéro. JZ peut ensuite utiliser cette condition pour choisir entre continuer séquentiellement et sauter vers une étiquette.</p>
        <div class="formula-box">CMP A, B → ZF = (A === B) → JZ LABEL</div>`,
      es: `<p>CMP no necesita almacenar un resultado en un registro de propósito general. En su lugar, registra si los dos operandos son iguales en el indicador cero. JZ puede entonces usar esa condición para elegir entre continuar secuencialmente o saltar a una etiqueta.</p>
        <div class="formula-box">CMP A, B → ZF = (A === B) → JZ ETIQUETA</div>`,
    },
    docLoopsBody: {
      en: `<p>A loop is created by combining a label, a state-changing instruction, a comparison and a conditional or unconditional jump. The countdown and sum examples demonstrate this pattern.</p>
        <ol><li>Update a register representing the loop state.</li><li>Compare it with a stopping condition.</li><li>Use JZ to leave the loop or JMP to repeat it.</li></ol>`,
      fr: `<p>Une boucle est créée en combinant une étiquette, une instruction qui modifie l'état, une comparaison et un saut conditionnel ou inconditionnel. Les exemples de compte à rebours et de somme illustrent ce schéma.</p>
        <ol><li>Mettre à jour un registre représentant l'état de la boucle.</li><li>Le comparer à une condition d'arrêt.</li><li>Utiliser JZ pour quitter la boucle ou JMP pour la répéter.</li></ol>`,
      es: `<p>Un bucle se crea combinando una etiqueta, una instrucción que cambia el estado, una comparación y un salto condicional o incondicional. Los ejemplos de cuenta regresiva y suma muestran este patrón.</p>
        <ol><li>Actualizar un registro que representa el estado del bucle.</li><li>Compararlo con una condición de parada.</li><li>Usar JZ para salir del bucle o JMP para repetirlo.</li></ol>`,
    },
    docLeavesOutBody: {
      en: `<p>This is intentionally a teaching model. A real processor adds many more details: instruction encoding, control logic, caches, buses, pipelining, branch prediction, interrupts, privilege levels and physical hardware timing.</p>
        <p>The simplified machine is useful because the same fundamental ideas remain visible: instructions change state, the PC drives control flow, registers hold working data, and memory stores persistent values.</p>`,
      fr: `<p>Il s'agit intentionnellement d'un modèle pédagogique. Un vrai processeur ajoute beaucoup plus de détails : encodage des instructions, logique de contrôle, caches, bus, pipelining, prédiction de branchement, interruptions, niveaux de privilège et timing matériel physique.</p>
        <p>La machine simplifiée est utile car les mêmes idées fondamentales restent visibles : les instructions modifient l'état, le PC pilote le flux de contrôle, les registres contiennent les données de travail, et la mémoire stocke les valeurs persistantes.</p>`,
      es: `<p>Este es intencionalmente un modelo didáctico. Un procesador real añade muchos más detalles: codificación de instrucciones, lógica de control, cachés, buses, segmentación, predicción de saltos, interrupciones, niveles de privilegio y sincronización física del hardware.</p>
        <p>La máquina simplificada es útil porque las mismas ideas fundamentales siguen siendo visibles: las instrucciones cambian el estado, el PC impulsa el flujo de control, los registros contienen datos de trabajo y la memoria almacena valores persistentes.</p>`,
    },
    docAssemblyBody: {
      en: `<p>Assembly exposes operations close to the processor's instruction model. Instead of expressing a high-level loop directly, you explicitly manipulate registers, compare values, store data and change the program counter.</p>`,
      fr: `<p>L'assembleur expose des opérations proches du modèle d'instructions du processeur. Plutôt que d'exprimer directement une boucle de haut niveau, vous manipulez explicitement les registres, comparez des valeurs, stockez des données et modifiez le compteur ordinal.</p>`,
      es: `<p>El ensamblador expone operaciones cercanas al modelo de instrucciones del procesador. En lugar de expresar directamente un bucle de alto nivel, manipulas explícitamente registros, comparas valores, almacenas datos y cambias el contador de programa.</p>`,
    },
  };

  let currentLang: LangCode = "en";

  try {
    const saved = localStorage.getItem(LANG_STORAGE_KEY);
    if (saved === "en" || saved === "fr" || saved === "es") {
      currentLang = saved;
    }
  } catch {
    // localStorage unavailable — fall back to English
  }

  function t(key: string, vars?: Record<string, string | number>): string {
    const entry = STATIC_TEXT[key];
    let str = entry ? entry[currentLang] ?? entry.en : key;

    if (vars) {
      for (const varKey in vars) {
        str = str.replace(new RegExp(`\\{${varKey}\\}`, "g"), String(vars[varKey]));
      }
    }

    return str;
  }

  function applyStaticTranslations(): void {
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-i18n]").forEach((element) => {
      const key = element.getAttribute("data-i18n");
      if (key && STATIC_TEXT[key]) {
        element.textContent = t(key);
      }
    });

    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-i18n-html]").forEach((element) => {
      const key = element.getAttribute("data-i18n-html");
      if (key && STATIC_HTML[key]) {
        element.innerHTML = STATIC_HTML[key][currentLang] ?? STATIC_HTML[key].en;
      }
    });

    document.documentElement.lang = currentLang;
  }

  function updateLangButtons(): void {
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>(".lang-btn").forEach((button) => {
      button.classList.toggle("active", button.dataset.lang === currentLang);
    });
  }

  const langChangeListeners: (() => void)[] = [];

  function onLangChange(listener: () => void): void {
    langChangeListeners.push(listener);
  }

  function setLanguage(lang: LangCode): void {
    if (lang === currentLang) {
      return;
    }

    currentLang = lang;

    try {
      localStorage.setItem(LANG_STORAGE_KEY, lang);
    } catch {
      // ignore storage failures
    }

    applyStaticTranslations();
    updateLangButtons();

    langChangeListeners.forEach((listener) => listener());
  }

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>(".lang-btn").forEach((button) => {
    button.addEventListener("click", () => {
      const lang = button.dataset.lang;
      if (lang === "en" || lang === "fr" || lang === "es") {
        setLanguage(lang);
      }
    });
  });

  applyStaticTranslations();
  updateLangButtons();

  /* ================================================================= */
  /* CPU SIMULATOR                                                      */
  /* ================================================================= */

  (function cpuModule() {
    const programEl = document.getElementById("cpu-program") as HTMLTextAreaElement;
    const exampleSelect = document.getElementById("cpu-example") as HTMLSelectElement;
    const loadExampleBtn = document.getElementById("cpu-load-example") as HTMLButtonElement;
    const registersEl = document.getElementById("cpu-registers");
    const cycleEl = document.getElementById("cpu-cycle");
    const assembleBtn = document.getElementById("cpu-assemble") as HTMLButtonElement;
    const stepBtn = document.getElementById("cpu-step") as HTMLButtonElement;
    const runBtn = document.getElementById("cpu-run") as HTMLButtonElement;
    const resetBtn = document.getElementById("cpu-reset") as HTMLButtonElement;
    const pcEl = document.getElementById("cpu-pc");
    const statusEl = document.getElementById("cpu-status");
    const memoryEl = document.getElementById("cpu-memory");
    const consoleEl = document.getElementById("cpu-console");
    const executionStages = document.querySelectorAll("[data-execution-stage]");
    const stepCountEl = document.getElementById("cpu-step-count");
    const currentAddressEl = document.getElementById("cpu-current-address");
    const currentInstructionEl = document.getElementById("cpu-current-instruction");
    const instructionEffectEl = document.getElementById("cpu-instruction-effect");
    const timelineEl = document.getElementById("cpu-timeline");

    if (!programEl || !exampleSelect || !loadExampleBtn || !registersEl || !cycleEl ||
        !assembleBtn || !stepBtn || !runBtn || !resetBtn || !pcEl || !statusEl ||
        !memoryEl || !consoleEl || !stepCountEl || !currentAddressEl ||
        !currentInstructionEl || !instructionEffectEl || !timelineEl) return;

    const REG_COUNT = 8;
    const MEM_SIZE = 32;

    type Instruction = { op: string; args: string[]; raw: string };

    let registers = new Array(REG_COUNT).fill(0);
    let memory = new Array(MEM_SIZE).fill(0);
    let program: Instruction[] = [];
    let pc = 0;
    let zeroFlag = false;
    let halted = true;
    let running = false;

    /* -------------------- dynamic i18n messages -------------------- */

    type StatusKey = "idle" | "assembled" | "ready" | "running" | "halted" | "error";
    let currentStatus: StatusKey = "idle";

    const statusMsg: Record<LangCode, Record<StatusKey, string>> = {
      en: { idle: "Idle", assembled: "Assembled", ready: "Ready", running: "Running", halted: "Halted", error: "Error" },
      fr: { idle: "Inactif", assembled: "Assemblé", ready: "Prêt", running: "En cours", halted: "Arrêté", error: "Erreur" },
      es: { idle: "Inactivo", assembled: "Ensamblado", ready: "Listo", running: "Ejecutando", halted: "Detenido", error: "Error" },
    };

    const cpuMsg: Record<LangCode, Record<string, string>> = {
      en: {
        logAssembled: "Assembled {count} instructions.",
        logMemoryWrite: "  memory[{addr}] = {val}",
        logError: "error: {msg}",
        logHalted: "Program halted.",
        haltEffect: "HALT completed — the CPU has stopped.",
        cyclePrefix: "CYCLE {n}",
        pcPrefix: "PC {n}",
        unknownLabel: "unknown label {label}",
        unknownInstruction: "unknown instruction {op}",
        effectMov: "Register {dest} receives {val}.",
        effectAdd: "Add {val} to {dest}.",
        effectSub: "Subtract {val} from {dest}.",
        effectLoad: "Read memory[{addr}] into {dest}.",
        effectStore: "Write {val} into memory[{addr}].",
        effectCmp: "Compare {a} with {b} → zero flag is updated.",
        effectJmp: "Jump to label {label}.",
        effectJz: "Jump to {label} only when the zero flag is set.",
        effectHalt: "Stop the processor.",
        effectDefault: "Execute instruction.",
      },
      fr: {
        logAssembled: "{count} instructions assemblées.",
        logMemoryWrite: "  mémoire[{addr}] = {val}",
        logError: "erreur : {msg}",
        logHalted: "Programme arrêté.",
        haltEffect: "HALT terminé — le CPU s'est arrêté.",
        cyclePrefix: "CYCLE {n}",
        pcPrefix: "PC {n}",
        unknownLabel: "étiquette inconnue {label}",
        unknownInstruction: "instruction inconnue {op}",
        effectMov: "Le registre {dest} reçoit {val}.",
        effectAdd: "Ajouter {val} à {dest}.",
        effectSub: "Soustraire {val} de {dest}.",
        effectLoad: "Lire mémoire[{addr}] vers {dest}.",
        effectStore: "Écrire {val} dans mémoire[{addr}].",
        effectCmp: "Comparer {a} avec {b} → le drapeau zéro est mis à jour.",
        effectJmp: "Sauter vers l'étiquette {label}.",
        effectJz: "Sauter vers {label} uniquement si le drapeau zéro est activé.",
        effectHalt: "Arrêter le processeur.",
        effectDefault: "Exécuter l'instruction.",
      },
      es: {
        logAssembled: "Se ensamblaron {count} instrucciones.",
        logMemoryWrite: "  memoria[{addr}] = {val}",
        logError: "error: {msg}",
        logHalted: "Programa detenido.",
        haltEffect: "HALT completado — la CPU se ha detenido.",
        cyclePrefix: "CICLO {n}",
        pcPrefix: "PC {n}",
        unknownLabel: "etiqueta desconocida {label}",
        unknownInstruction: "instrucción desconocida {op}",
        effectMov: "El registro {dest} recibe {val}.",
        effectAdd: "Sumar {val} a {dest}.",
        effectSub: "Restar {val} de {dest}.",
        effectLoad: "Leer memoria[{addr}] hacia {dest}.",
        effectStore: "Escribir {val} en memoria[{addr}].",
        effectCmp: "Comparar {a} con {b} → se actualiza el indicador cero.",
        effectJmp: "Saltar a la etiqueta {label}.",
        effectJz: "Saltar a {label} solo si el indicador cero está activado.",
        effectHalt: "Detener el procesador.",
        effectDefault: "Ejecutar instrucción.",
      },
    };

    function cpuT(key: string, vars?: Record<string, string | number>): string {
      let str = cpuMsg[currentLang][key] ?? cpuMsg.en[key];
      if (vars) {
        for (const varKey in vars) {
          str = str.replace(new RegExp(`\\{${varKey}\\}`, "g"), String(vars[varKey]));
        }
      }
      return str;
    }

    function setStatus(status: StatusKey) {
      currentStatus = status;
      statusEl!.textContent = statusMsg[currentLang][status];
    }

    const examples: Record<string, string> = {
      sum: [
        "MOV R0, 0    ; sum",
        "MOV R1, 1    ; counter",
        "MOV R2, 5    ; limit",
        "LOOP:",
        "CMP R1, R2",
        "JZ END",
        "ADD R0, R1",
        "ADD R1, 1",
        "JMP LOOP",
        "END:",
        "ADD R0, R2   ; include the limit itself",
        "STORE R0, 0",
        "HALT",
      ].join("\n"),
      loop: [
        "MOV R0, 5",
        "LOOP:",
        "STORE R0, R0",
        "SUB R0, 1",
        "CMP R0, 0",
        "JZ END",
        "JMP LOOP",
        "END:",
        "HALT",
      ].join("\n"),
      fib: [
        "MOV R0, 0    ; fib(0)",
        "MOV R1, 1    ; fib(1)",
        "MOV R2, 0    ; index",
        "STORE R0, R2",
        "LOOP:",
        "ADD R2, 1",
        "CMP R2, 6",
        "JZ END",
        "MOV R3, R1",
        "ADD R1, R0",
        "MOV R0, R3",
        "STORE R1, R2",
        "JMP LOOP",
        "END:",
        "HALT",
      ].join("\n"),
    };

    function log(text: string, cls = "") {
      const line = document.createElement("div");
      line.className = "cpu-console-line" + (cls ? ` ${cls}` : "");
      line.textContent = text;
      consoleEl!.appendChild(line);
      consoleEl!.scrollTop = consoleEl!.scrollHeight;
    }

    function renderRegisters(activeIdx: number | null) {
      registersEl!.innerHTML = "";
      registers.forEach((val, i) => {
        const cell = document.createElement("div");
        cell.className = "cpu-register" + (i === activeIdx ? " active" : "");
        cell.innerHTML = `<div class="cpu-register-label">R${i}</div><div class="cpu-register-value">${val}</div>`;
        registersEl!.appendChild(cell);
      });
    }

    function renderMemory(activeAddr: number | null) {
      memoryEl!.innerHTML = "";
      memory.forEach((val, i) => {
        const cell = document.createElement("div");
        cell.className = "cpu-cell" + (i === activeAddr ? " active" : "");
        cell.innerHTML = `<div class="cpu-cell-addr">${i}</div><div class="cpu-cell-value">${val}</div>`;
        memoryEl!.appendChild(cell);
      });
    }

    function setCycleStep(step: "fetch" | "decode" | "execute" | null) {
      cycleEl!.querySelectorAll(".cpu-cycle-step").forEach((el) => {
        el.classList.toggle("active", el.getAttribute("data-step") === step);
      });
    }

    let cycleNumber = 0;
    let lastPc: number | null = null;

    function setExecutionStage(stage: "fetch" | "decode" | "execute" | null) {
      executionStages.forEach((el) => {
        const elStage = el.getAttribute("data-execution-stage");
        el.classList.toggle("active", elStage === stage);
        el.classList.toggle(
          "done",
          stage !== null &&
          ["fetch", "decode", "execute"].indexOf(elStage || "") <
            ["fetch", "decode", "execute"].indexOf(stage)
        );
      });
      setCycleStep(stage);
    }

    function describeEffect(instr: Instruction): string {
      switch (instr.op) {
        case "MOV":
          return cpuT("effectMov", { dest: instr.args[0], val: instr.args[1] });
        case "ADD":
          return cpuT("effectAdd", { val: instr.args[1], dest: instr.args[0] });
        case "SUB":
          return cpuT("effectSub", { val: instr.args[1], dest: instr.args[0] });
        case "LOAD":
          return cpuT("effectLoad", { addr: instr.args[1], dest: instr.args[0] });
        case "STORE":
          return cpuT("effectStore", { val: instr.args[0], addr: instr.args[1] });
        case "CMP":
          return cpuT("effectCmp", { a: instr.args[0], b: instr.args[1] });
        case "JMP":
          return cpuT("effectJmp", { label: instr.args[0] });
        case "JZ":
          return cpuT("effectJz", { label: instr.args[0] });
        case "HALT":
          return cpuT("effectHalt");
        default:
          return cpuT("effectDefault");
      }
    }

    function renderTimeline(activePc: number | null = null) {
      timelineEl!.innerHTML = "";

      if (!program.length) {
        const empty = document.createElement("div");
        empty.className = "timeline-empty";
        empty.textContent = t("timelineEmpty");
        timelineEl!.appendChild(empty);
        return;
      }

      program.forEach((instr, i) => {
        const item = document.createElement("div");
        item.className =
          "timeline-item" +
          (i === activePc ? " active" : "") +
          (lastPc !== null && i < lastPc ? " executed" : "");

        const pcSpan = document.createElement("span");
        pcSpan.className = "timeline-pc";
        pcSpan.textContent = cpuT("pcPrefix", { n: String(i).padStart(2, "0") });

        const op = document.createElement("strong");
        op.className = "timeline-op";
        op.textContent = instr.op;

        const raw = document.createElement("span");
        raw.className = "timeline-raw";
        raw.textContent = instr.raw;

        item.append(pcSpan, op, raw);
        timelineEl!.appendChild(item);
      });

      const active = timelineEl!.querySelector(".timeline-item.active") as HTMLElement | null;
      active?.scrollIntoView({ behavior: "smooth", block: "nearest", inline: "center" });
    }

    function showCurrentInstruction(index: number | null) {
      if (index === null || !program[index]) {
        currentAddressEl!.textContent = cpuT("pcPrefix", { n: "00" });
        currentInstructionEl!.textContent = t("waitingForProgram");
        instructionEffectEl!.textContent = t("instructionEffectDefault");
        instructionEffectEl!.classList.remove("changed");
        renderTimeline(null);
        return;
      }

      const instr = program[index];
      currentAddressEl!.textContent = cpuT("pcPrefix", { n: String(index).padStart(2, "0") });
      currentInstructionEl!.textContent = instr.raw;
      instructionEffectEl!.textContent = describeEffect(instr);
      instructionEffectEl!.classList.add("changed");
      renderTimeline(index);
    }

    function resolveOperand(token: string): number {
      token = token.trim();
      if (token.startsWith("R") && !isNaN(Number(token.slice(1)))) {
        return registers[Number(token.slice(1))];
      }
      return Number(token);
    }

    function regIndex(token: string): number {
      return Number(token.trim().slice(1));
    }

    function assemble(source: string): { ok: boolean; error?: string } {
      const rawLines = source.split("\n").map((l) => l.split(";")[0].trim()).filter(Boolean);
      const labels: Record<string, number> = {};
      const instructions: Instruction[] = [];

      rawLines.forEach((line) => {
        if (line.endsWith(":")) {
          labels[line.slice(0, -1).trim()] = instructions.length;
        } else {
          const [op, ...rest] = line.split(/\s+/);
          const args = rest.join(" ").split(",").map((a) => a.trim()).filter(Boolean);
          instructions.push({ op: op.toUpperCase(), args, raw: line });
        }
      });

      // Resolve label references stored as strings; validated at execute time.
      (instructions as any).labels = labels;
      program = instructions;
      return { ok: true };
    }

    function resetMachine(keepProgram: boolean) {
      registers = new Array(REG_COUNT).fill(0);
      memory = new Array(MEM_SIZE).fill(0);
      pc = 0;
      zeroFlag = false;
      halted = !keepProgram ? true : halted;
      if (!keepProgram) program = [];
      renderRegisters(null);
      renderMemory(null);
      setCycleStep(null);
      pcEl!.textContent = "0";
      setStatus(keepProgram ? "assembled" : "idle");
      cycleNumber = 0;
      lastPc = null;
      stepCountEl!.textContent = cpuT("cyclePrefix", { n: 0 });
      setExecutionStage(null);
      showCurrentInstruction(keepProgram && program.length ? 0 : null);
    }

    function labelsOf(prog: Instruction[]): Record<string, number> {
      return (prog as any).labels || {};
    }

    async function step(): Promise<boolean> {
      if (halted || pc >= program.length) {
        halted = true;
        setStatus("halted");
        stepBtn.disabled = true;
        runBtn.disabled = true;
        return false;
      }

      setExecutionStage("fetch");
      pcEl!.textContent = String(pc);
      showCurrentInstruction(pc);
      await sleep(300);

      const instr = program[pc];
      setExecutionStage("decode");
      log(`[${pc}] ${instr.raw}`);
      await sleep(300);

      setExecutionStage("execute");
      await sleep(300);

      const labels = labelsOf(program);
      let nextPc = pc + 1;

      try {
        switch (instr.op) {
          case "MOV": {
            const dest = regIndex(instr.args[0]);
            registers[dest] = resolveOperand(instr.args[1]);
            renderRegisters(dest);
            break;
          }
          case "ADD": {
            const dest = regIndex(instr.args[0]);
            registers[dest] += resolveOperand(instr.args[1]);
            renderRegisters(dest);
            break;
          }
          case "SUB": {
            const dest = regIndex(instr.args[0]);
            registers[dest] -= resolveOperand(instr.args[1]);
            renderRegisters(dest);
            break;
          }
          case "LOAD": {
            const dest = regIndex(instr.args[0]);
            const addr = resolveOperand(instr.args[1]);
            registers[dest] = memory[addr] ?? 0;
            renderRegisters(dest);
            renderMemory(addr);
            break;
          }
          case "STORE": {
            const val = resolveOperand(instr.args[0]);
            const addr = resolveOperand(instr.args[1]);
            if (addr >= 0 && addr < MEM_SIZE) memory[addr] = val;
            renderMemory(addr);
            log(cpuT("logMemoryWrite", { addr, val }), "out");
            break;
          }
          case "CMP": {
            const a = resolveOperand(instr.args[0]);
            const b = resolveOperand(instr.args[1]);
            zeroFlag = a === b;
            break;
          }
          case "JMP": {
            const target = labels[instr.args[0]];
            if (target === undefined) throw new Error(cpuT("unknownLabel", { label: instr.args[0] }));
            nextPc = target;
            break;
          }
          case "JZ": {
            if (zeroFlag) {
              const target = labels[instr.args[0]];
              if (target === undefined) throw new Error(cpuT("unknownLabel", { label: instr.args[0] }));
              nextPc = target;
            }
            break;
          }
          case "HALT": {
            halted = true;
            break;
          }
          default:
            throw new Error(cpuT("unknownInstruction", { op: instr.op }));
        }
      } catch (e) {
        log(cpuT("logError", { msg: (e as Error).message }), "err");
        halted = true;
        setStatus("error");
        stepBtn.disabled = true;
        runBtn.disabled = true;
        return false;
      }

      await sleep(300);
      lastPc = pc;
      pc = nextPc;
      cycleNumber += 1;
      stepCountEl!.textContent = cpuT("cyclePrefix", { n: cycleNumber });

      if (halted) {
        setExecutionStage("execute");
        currentInstructionEl!.textContent = instr.raw;
        instructionEffectEl!.textContent = cpuT("haltEffect");
        instructionEffectEl!.classList.add("changed");
        setStatus("halted");
        log(cpuT("logHalted"), "out");
        stepBtn.disabled = true;
        runBtn.disabled = true;
        return false;
      }

      setStatus("running");
      return true;
    }

    assembleBtn.addEventListener("click", () => {
      resetMachine(false);
      const result = assemble(programEl.value);
      if (result.ok) {
        halted = false;
        pc = 0;
        stepBtn.disabled = false;
        runBtn.disabled = false;
        consoleEl!.innerHTML = "";
        log(cpuT("logAssembled", { count: program.length }));
        renderRegisters(null);
        renderMemory(null);
        setStatus("ready");
        cycleNumber = 0;
        lastPc = null;
        stepCountEl!.textContent = cpuT("cyclePrefix", { n: 0 });
        setExecutionStage(null);
        showCurrentInstruction(0);
      }
    });

    stepBtn.addEventListener("click", () => { void step(); });

    runBtn.addEventListener("click", async () => {
      if (running) return;
      running = true;
      stepBtn.disabled = true;
      let alive = true;
      while (alive && !halted) {
        alive = await step();
      }
      running = false;
    });

    resetBtn.addEventListener("click", () => {
      resetMachine(false);
      consoleEl!.innerHTML = "";
      stepBtn.disabled = true;
      runBtn.disabled = true;
      setExecutionStage(null);
      showCurrentInstruction(null);
      stepCountEl!.textContent = cpuT("cyclePrefix", { n: 0 });
    });

    loadExampleBtn.addEventListener("click", () => {
      programEl.value = examples[exampleSelect.value];
    });

    onLangChange(() => {
      setStatus(currentStatus);
      stepCountEl!.textContent = cpuT("cyclePrefix", { n: cycleNumber });
      showCurrentInstruction(program.length && lastPc !== null ? Math.min(pc, program.length - 1) : (program.length ? pc : null));
    });

    programEl.value = examples.sum;
    resetMachine(false);
  })();
</script>